        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.eveonline.com/lesican/{size}/448285_2.png",
        "created_at": "2025-01-14T17:59:47.134Z",
        "cooked": "<p>let me explain</p>\n<p>person has 2 accounts, creates an alt on each and runs the air career program, this puts skill points into the redeem queue for the main character. every 10 hours these toons can be deleted and the process repeated.</p>\n<p>as they do this over weeks they change their strategy to optimise the time it takes to get the skill points, human learning</p>\n<p>things like duelling each other for the soldier of fortune part, or warp to 5 anomalies for the explorer path.</p>\n<p>I am not saying it is or isn’t botting, or if doing the npe a billion times a month is good for the game but nothing you described is against the rules</p>",
